BRL-CAD Blender reader
======================

The reader parses Blender's self-describing binary project format directly.  It
does not link to Blender or use Blender source code.  The implementation reads
the file header and block table, decodes the embedded SDNA schema, resolves old
memory addresses within bounded file blocks, and accesses geometry by SDNA
field name rather than host-language structure layouts.

Geometry support
----------------

* 32-bit and 64-bit pointer encodings
* little-endian and big-endian files
* uncompressed and gzip-compressed files
* object instances and their world transformation matrices
* legacy MVert/MFace meshes
* MVert/MLoop/MPoly meshes
* attribute-backed meshes using position, corner-vertex, and face-offset data
* concave polygon triangulation using libbg ear clipping

Meshes are written as unoriented BRL-CAD BOT primitives.  Materials, animation,
modifiers, and non-mesh object data do not affect the imported geometry.  The
reader reports unsupported object data types and malformed or unresolved data
instead of interpreting unknown layouts speculatively.  Zstandard-compressed
files and the extended header introduced after Blender 4.x are recognized but
not currently decoded.

Format references
-----------------

The implementation was informed by the following independently published
descriptions and permissively licensed references:

* Library of Congress, "Blender 3D Data File (BLEND)," fdd000559.
* Kaitai Struct format gallery, ".blend file format of Blender" (CC0-1.0).
* Jeroen Bakker, "The mystery of the blend" binary-format notes.
* Open Asset Import Library Blender importer and test corpus (BSD-3-Clause).

No GPL source code or GPL parsing library is used by this plugin.
